# docking_benchmark.kfl: a six-degree-of-freedom docking task.
#
# A ten-tonne class crew vehicle holds station ten metres off a large
# station's docking interface and has to close, stay inside the
# capture envelope its port declares, and mate. Translation is flown
# on twelve thrusters and attitude on three reaction wheels, and both
# have to be right at the same instant, which is what makes this one
# task rather than an approach and a pointing problem side by side.
#
# The initial state is not a hand-computed state vector. The chaser
# sits at the station-keeping hold point of the linearised relative
# motion, 47.35 m ahead along the direction of travel, which is the
# offset that leaves the mating planes ten metres apart. A craft held
# there needs no relative velocity in the rotating frame, so its world
# velocity is the station's plus the frame's own rotation across the
# offset, which is 0.0536549 m/s inward.
#
# Free drift does not dock. Closing along the direction of travel
# drives a radial acceleration of twice the mean motion times the
# closing rate, and what that builds up depends on how long the
# approach lasts: flown at the envelope's own 0.07 m/sec the approach
# takes about 140 seconds and carries the chaser about 1.6 m off the
# docking axis, sixteen times the envelope's lateral misalignment
# limit. The lateral thrusters are what answer that, and the wheels
# are what answer the initial angular rate: left alone, the rate the
# reset draws turns the vehicle by far more than the four degrees the
# envelope admits.
#
# The four outcomes are the ones the task has, and each is an ordinary
# ending rather than a special case. Docked: the contact satisfied
# every condition and `dock_captured` is set. Impact: contact anywhere
# else, or a port contact outside the envelope, ends the episode with
# that channel clear. Horizon: the declared horizon truncates. Fault:
# the physics could not advance honestly, which nothing in this task
# introduces.
#
# The reward is written against the same envelope the outcome is
# judged by, because a reward and a success condition that disagree
# are settled in the reward's favour: the reward is collected every
# step and the condition once. Its largest term tracks a closing rate
# rather than paying for one. The rate it asks for is the middle of
# the envelope's closing-rate band, 0.075 m/sec, plus four hundredths
# of the range still to run, so it is 0.475 m/sec at the hold point
# and falls onto the middle of the band exactly as the interfaces
# meet, which takes about 50 seconds rather than 140. The reference
# is proportional to the range with no ceiling on purpose. A term
# that simply paid for closing speed asks for the opposite, since
# more speed is always worth more and it goes on asking at the mating
# plane; and a reference held below a ceiling has a flat stretch that
# a policy can sit on without ever having to brake.
#
# The remaining terms are the four alignment residuals and their four
# rates, each weighted by the reciprocal of its own limit in that
# envelope, so that each costs about one unit of reward per step at
# that limit and the angular rates carry the largest coefficients.
# That is what makes the reward and the capture test agree about
# which residual is the binding one. A small range term keeps
# standing off from ever being free.
#
# The closing-rate term is heavier than that same rule would make it,
# and deliberately so. It is the only term carrying a schedule, and
# following a schedule costs steps: a craft that ignores it and
# arrives early pays every one of the other terms fewer times. The
# rate term therefore has to be worth more than the steps that
# patience adds, and at one unit per step it is not. Weighted at one
# unit per step it buys an arrival at the rate the approach began
# with; weighted as it is here it buys the braking.
#
# The capture is paid once and the shaping is paid every step, so the
# capture has to be worth the steps a careful approach spends: it is
# worth several times what a whole approach accumulates. Nothing flat
# is paid at the end. A constant added to every ending is added to
# the capture as well, and separates none of them.
#
# The vehicles are `examples/assets/crew_vehicle_10t.k26asm` and
# `examples/assets/space_station.k26asm`, and every number in both
# carries its provenance in the asset's own bytes.

form DOCKING_BENCHMARK
title "Six-degree-of-freedom docking benchmark"
size 320x200

fn world docking_world
    astro_body earth gm=3.986004418e14 mass=5.972e24 radius=6.371e6
    astro_body station assembly="assets/space_station.k26asm" parent=earth pos_x=6771000.0 pos_y=0.0 pos_z=0.0 vel_x=0.0 vel_y=7672.5986483850129 vel_z=0.0 quat_w=0.5 quat_x=0.5 quat_y=0.5 quat_z=0.5 omega_x=0.0 omega_y=0.0011331559073083758 omega_z=0.0
    astro_body chaser assembly="assets/crew_vehicle_10t.k26asm" parent=earth pos_x=6771000.0 pos_y=47.35 pos_z=0.0 vel_x=-0.053654932211051595 vel_y=7672.5986483850129 vel_z=0.0 quat_w=0.5 quat_x=0.5 quat_y=-0.5 quat_z=-0.5 omega_x=0.0 omega_y=0.0011331559073083758 omega_z=0.0

    episode
        control_dt 0.5
        substeps 5
        horizon 400
        terminated when touch_hit > 0.5
        reset chaser.pos_x uniform(6770999.5, 6771000.5)
        reset chaser.pos_z uniform(-0.5, 0.5)
        reset chaser.vel_z uniform(-0.002, 0.002)
        reset chaser.quat_z uniform(-0.52, -0.48)
        reset chaser.omega_z uniform(-0.002, 0.002)
    end

    action close box 0.0 1.0 default 0.0
    action brake box 0.0 1.0 default 0.0
    action lat_yp box 0.0 1.0 default 0.0
    action lat_ym box 0.0 1.0 default 0.0
    action lat_zp box 0.0 1.0 default 0.0
    action lat_zm box 0.0 1.0 default 0.0
    action tq_x box -1.0 1.0 default 0.0
    action tq_y box -1.0 1.0 default 0.0
    action tq_z box -1.0 1.0 default 0.0

    # The navigation sensor the relative state is read through. The
    # true values travel beside the measured ones so a privileged
    # critic and the record can see both.
    sensor nav
        noise normal 0.0 0.01
        latency 1
    end

    on_step
        chaser.close_yp.throttle = close
        chaser.close_ym.throttle = close
        chaser.brake_yp.throttle = brake
        chaser.brake_ym.throttle = brake
        chaser.lat_yp_fwd.throttle = lat_yp
        chaser.lat_yp_aft.throttle = lat_yp
        chaser.lat_ym_fwd.throttle = lat_ym
        chaser.lat_ym_aft.throttle = lat_ym
        chaser.lat_zp_fwd.throttle = lat_zp
        chaser.lat_zp_aft.throttle = lat_zp
        chaser.lat_zm_fwd.throttle = lat_zm
        chaser.lat_zm_aft.throttle = lat_zm
        chaser.wheel_x.torque = 5.0 * tq_x
        chaser.wheel_y.torque = 5.0 * tq_y
        chaser.wheel_z.torque = 5.0 * tq_z
    end

    observe relative station from chaser through nav with truth as rel
    observe attitude of chaser as att
    observe attitude of station as sta
    observe port forward of chaser as dock
    observe contact of chaser as touch

    objective
        reward -150.0 * abs(dock_v_axial - (0.075 + 0.04 * dock_axial)) - 0.05 * dock_axial - 10.0 * dock_lateral - 14.0 * dock_pitchyaw - 14.0 * dock_roll - 25.0 * dock_v_lateral - 280.0 * dock_v_pitchyaw - 280.0 * dock_v_roll
        terminal 2000.0 * dock_captured
    end
end
end
